{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>The poor man.</b> Some say that המסכן is like סוכן (Isaiah 22:15), the one appointed over storehouses, and likewise המסכן is one who administers over a terumah-offering. But the correct interpretation is that it is an adjective [for the wood] that is stored away in a treasury, being a terumah-offering to make an idol from it:" "<b>He chooses.</b> The owner of the terumah-offering:" "<b>It will not move.</b> To fasten it with nails:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {0 "The bracketed [העץ] ('the wood') appears in the source text; retained as bracketed editorial insertion."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:11.417656200Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}